erson’s behaviour in this situation.","Choose **are being**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The continuous of be requires being after are.","B":"A finite auxiliary is missing.","C":"**Are being helpful** describes the person’s behaviour in this situation.","D":"Is does not agree with you."}}},{"id":"df11f915-e5a3-5381-a57b-7d5d8333587c","topicSlug":"stative-dynamic","level":"B1","prompt":"Describe present knowledge: “I ____ how to translate the travel leaflet.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"am knowing"},{"id":"B","text":"knowing"},{"id":"C","text":"am know"},{"id":"D","text":"know"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"The sentence expresses **knowledge**, not an activity in progress.","explanation":"Knowledge is a state in this sentence, so the ordinary form is **know**.","keywords":["knowledge-state"],"skill":"knowledge-state","contextKey":"stative-dynamic-4","fingerprint":"d9dd49782f608bc70abff16c3d1d4e4634cbf6b2d2e486e6ec4d47c827c6520d","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-stative"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The sentence expresses **knowledge**, not an activity in progress.","Knowledge is a state in this sentence, so the ordinary form is **know**.","Choose **know**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The ordinary possession-of-knowledge sense does not use continuous aspect.","B":"An -ing form alone is not a finite verb.","C":"Am cannot directly take the base verb know here.","D":"Knowledge is a state in this sentence, so the ordinary form is **know**."}}},{"id":"3b57e3f3-0821-50ba-ab5e-a5364b66c36b","topicSlug":"stative-dynamic","level":"B1","prompt":"Use present continuous for active consideration: “We ____ about how to translate the travel leaflet.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"is thinking"},{"id":"B","text":"are thinking"},{"id":"C","text":"are think"},{"id":"D","text":"thinking"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"Thinking about an issue is an **activity**; build the requested continuous form.","explanation":"Active consideration is dynamic: **are thinking about**.","keywords":["active-consideration"],"skill":"active-consideration","contextKey":"stative-dynamic-4","fingerprint":"23ed789206110849f7cc7b5614d228c7b1633fae1df7bb219647b13ffcc59e00","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-stative"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Thinking about an issue is an **activity**; build the requested continuous form.","Active consideration is dynamic: **are thinking about**.","Choose **are thinking**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Is does not agree with we.","B":"Active consideration is dynamic: **are thinking about**.","C":"The continuous requires thinking after are.","D":"The finite auxiliary are is missing."}}},{"id":"7942fb92-8ee6-5ca2-aa67-42f6a85a7008","topicSlug":"stative-dynamic","level":"B1","prompt":"State an opinion, in the simple present: “She ____ that translating the travel leaflet is worthwhile.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"thinking"},{"id":"B","text":"thinks"},{"id":"C","text":"think"},{"id":"D","text":"is think"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"Think followed by **that + proposition** expresses an opinion in this example.","explanation":"Think here means **hold an opinion**, so use simple present thinks with she.","keywords":["opinion-state"],"skill":"opinion-state","contextKey":"stative-dynamic-4","fingerprint":"35d68d615ceef85315944139de90185e0346c3ef10e852efe5afd1ba4260acbf","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-stative"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"